  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Cardinal Infrastructure benefits from strong construction demand, a healthy backlog, and aggressive regional expansion. Its new asphalt facility in North Carolina marks a strategic push into materials production, supporting vertical integration and cost improvement. Broader infrastructure trends fuel momentum, although inflation, potential rate hikes, and acquisition integration pose risks. Sharp recent share-price swings add near-term uncertainty, but the fundamental trajectory appears intact.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a consolidation strategy, acquiring ALGC and Piedmont Pipe to create an integrated, efficient platform. An upsized equity offering signals confidence and provides capital for further expansion. Analyst sentiment leans bullish, with several price-target increases; a recent upgrade back to “Strong-Buy” after the stock’s pullback implies that the market sees the decline as a buying opportunity rather than a fundamental issue.",
